{"content":[{"c":["MERATHAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name that Jeremiah uses in reference to God’s judgment upon Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.50.21","r":"Jer.50.21","rawR":"Jer.50.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.50.21","value":"Jer.50.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 50:21"},"). Though it means “double rebellion” or “twofold rebel,” it is a wordplay on the name for southern Babylonia, Marratu. Thus, God says, “Go up against the land, Two-fold rebel . . . and utterly destroy it!”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Merathaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 50:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.50.21","rawQueryValue":"Jer.50.21","sourceRefExact":"Jer.50.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8544a8c79ba0799fc49db02609c5e9425b6bb21bf4ea09e8900f3df7e2494dab","sourceItemName":"Merathaim","sourceItemOrder":253,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Merathaim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Merathaim","title":"Merathaim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}